{"title":"2015 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">2015 CEMC Pascal #18</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">2015 CEMC Cayley #16</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a magic square, the numbers in each row, the numbers in each column, and the numbers on each diagonal have the same sum. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>In the magic square shown, the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de683787ff4f0209012b2de9e0ff7bc4a3898c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 49 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 54 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 47 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the middle row and the diagonal with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5aed1ee15fb2876570e1b81c7422c041de7168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 + c + 11 = b + c + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9f30c97f338c3c2c812efb32bd30f75536c8a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + 30 = c + 12 + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff76d75e300e4fd396d418c2aef249c39af090b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = (c + 30) - (c + 12) = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We could have also used the leftmost column and the top row to figure this out\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>From the rightmost column, we see that the sum must be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4ba5d6100f49ad1a2efb2236238573f18cf8365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 11 + 16 = 29 + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Using this and the diagonal with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc8387111ef43e8a2b186bd1c351c59ef9d52d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c + 16 = 29 + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427c6d6c4f97659ba472eb293023d6e8474a8333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c = 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0ec9e2cd94979e1a88a3a3e1809e5c0d725f1c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3dac8cbb325309ba72b6f6133176e297d057235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 29 + 18 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 47}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"243\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>To confirm our answer, we can also fill the entire magic square.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2015 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 19 (page does n